+/*
+ * Orange Pi 5 Plus: mount the payload's Data volume on /private/var before the first exec of the init
+ * program.
+ *
+ * launchd needs a writable /private/var -- its swap file and the dyld shared-region cache live there -- and
+ * the OS volume of an IPSW is read-only. The payload hands a 32 MiB APFS seed over in RAM; package/NativeSd
+ * publishes it as a writable block device (boot-arg sd-data-ram=1) and APFS mounts its container. The VFS
+ * mount is the part that has to happen here: the APFS mount payload holds a user pointer to the device
+ * string, so it is built in the scratch page of process 1 and mount(2) is called on it, exactly as
+ * UniXNU-evb10's userland hook does for its own Data volume.
